  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward drift bias when recent history shows a spike (e.g., >86) followed by volatility; true outcomes immediately reverse direction with high frequency.",
    "Forecast horizon is structurally misaligned with market reality: model assumes linear continuation while actual EU ETS prices exhibit mean-reverting V-shapes within 5-10 days.",
    "Sentiment history (near-zero or slightly negative) fails to trigger downward correction in the model, leading to significant overshoots above true peaks.",
    "When recent high prices are followed by a drop in sentiment or neutral sentiment, the model should apply a mean-reversion coefficient of -15% to its projected trajectory.",
    "Model ignores the 'volatility clustering' effect where a single spike is immediately followed by a rapid consolidation and reversal, treating it as a trend start instead."
  ]
}
